    "notes": [
      "EN RC delay (10 kohm to 3V3, 1 uF to GND; the datasheet leaves the values to the power-up timing and recommends these); the RESET button pulls EN to GND.",
      "BOOT: IO9 to GND through a button (the datasheet shows a jumper): held at reset = download mode; IO8 pulled up (10 kohm) so download mode works.",
      "USB: IO12 = D-, IO13 = D+ to a USB connector (series resistors and capacitors to GND reserved near the module, values left open); USB Serial/JTAG flashes and logs without a bridge chip.",
      "Optional 32.768 kHz crystal on IO0/IO1 with 12 pF load capacitors (not fitted by default)."
    ],
    "page": "9 Peripheral Schematics (p. 40)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Supply: 3.0-3.6 V able to deliver 500 mA; 22 uF and 100 nF at the 3V3 pin.",
    "Strapping pins sampled at reset: IO9 (weak pull-up; low = download mode, the BOOT button), IO8 (floating; must be high for download mode: 10 kohm pull-up), IO4/IO5 (SDIO edges, floating), IO15 (JTAG source, read only when an eFuse enables it). Do not load them with circuits that pull the wrong way during reset.",
    "Every GPIO reaches UART, SPI, I2C, I2S, LEDC PWM, MCPWM, PCNT, TWAI (CAN; needs an external transceiver) and RMT through the GPIO matrix; ADC1 on IO0-IO6; LP I2C on IO6/IO7, LP UART on IO4/IO5.",
    "Pins 36-53 and 1, 2, 11, 14 are ground pads: connect them all; NC pads stay unconnected.",
    "Antenna: the antenna area is the top 5.4 mm of the module (the edge with ground pads 36-48). The footprint keeps tracks, vias, pours and other parts out of the antenna area itself (the module's width plus 0.5 mm, and 0.5 mm beyond its edge), the minimum the datasheet marks as the keepout zone. The vendor's hardware design guidelines (Positioning a Module on a Base Board) strongly recommend the antenna outside the base board, or its feed point at the board edge with the board cut away beside and below it, and at least 15 mm of clearance around it in the product: place the module at a board edge with the antenna overhanging it (`place = [edge(.top, overhang = 5.4mm)]`: the rule's `overhang` is a Length, how far beyond the edge), keep copper and parts as far from the antenna as the board allows, and put ground copper with dense ground vias on the board near (not under) the antenna."
  ],
